[C] spurious non-additivity injected into the task:coverage interaction
    n_item = 48 per (task, coverage) cell, 4000 draws, shared across all 10 seeds
    compare against the ADOPTED P1 non-additivity RMS = 0.352767 (ADR-052 decision 2)
    s2_item    s2_tmpl    spurious RMS       as % of P1
    0.00       0.00       0.00000            0.00%
    0.00       0.50       0.00000            0.00%
    0.00       2.00       0.00000            0.00%
    0.00       8.00       0.00000            0.00%
    0.50       0.00       0.09847            27.92%
    1.00       0.00       0.13893            39.38%
    2.00       0.00       0.19538            55.38%
    4.00       0.00       0.27600            78.24%
    1.00       1.00       0.13812            39.15%
    4.00       4.00       0.27693            78.50%
    -> `s2_tmpl` contributes EXACTLY 0: the same template index serves the same
       item index in every coverage cell, so it cancels in the interaction.
       That cancellation is a property of the cycling assignment (ADR-069 decision 4 (3)).
    -> `s2_item` does NOT cancel, and it does NOT shrink with n_seed:
       v[item] is drawn once and shared across all 10 seeds (draw_frame).

    CONTROL -- the same metric applied to the SEED term (sigma, rho):
    sigma      rho        spurious RMS       as % of P1
    0.00       0.00       0.00000            0.00%
    0.50       0.00       0.00000            0.00%
    1.50       0.00       0.00000            0.00%
    1.50       1.00       0.00000            0.00%
    -> also EXACTLY 0: `u[s, cov]` carries no task index (ADR-066 decision 4 (d)),
       so it shifts all four task types alike and drops out of the interaction.
    -> READ THIS NARROWLY.  This channel is the DIRECT contribution to the 12 cell
       means only.  sigma still costs power through the binomial sampling channel
       (link nonlinearity), which check 2 measured (F108) and this check does NOT.
       The point is the ASYMMETRY: of the three variance components, only
       `s2_item` feeds the task:coverage interaction directly.

[D] how the s2_item contribution scales with n_item (`M*` = junjo5, pending)
    s2_item = 1.0 fixed; s2_tmpl = 0
    n_item     spurious RMS       as % of P1
    12         0.27741            78.64%
    24         0.19512            55.31%
    48         0.13802            39.13%
    96         0.09865            27.97%
    192        0.06898            19.55%
    384        0.04887            13.85%
    -> falls as 1/sqrt(n_item).  `n_item` is null until `M*` lands (junjo5),
       so the stakes of the s2_item choice are themselves `M*`-dependent.

